+# Development Guide
+
+This repository uses **Git submodules** to include [Lite3_rl_deploy](https://github.com/HaifaUnivSAIL/Lite3_rl_deploy) as a dependency.  
+That means you can work on `Lite3_rl_training` and `Lite3_rl_deploy` side-by-side, but changes to `Lite3_rl_deploy` live in **your fork** (not the upstream repo).
+
+### Workflow: editing and pushing code
+
+1. **Enter the submodule**
+   ```bash
+   cd Lite3/Lite3_rl_deploy
+   ```
+
+2. **Check you’re on the right branch**
+   ```bash
+   git status
+   # should show: On branch main
+   ```
+
+3. **Make your code changes**  
+   Add new files, edit sources, etc.
+
+4. **Commit inside the submodule**
+   ```bash
+   git add -A
+   git commit -m "Describe your change here"
+   ```
+
+5. **Push to your fork**
+   ```bash
+   git push origin main
+   ```
+   > :information_source: `origin` is already set to your fork (`HaifaUnivSAIL/Lite3_rl_deploy`).
+
+6. **Pin the new submodule commit in the umbrella repo**
+   Go back to the top level of `Lite3`:
+   ```bash
+   cd ..
+   git add Lite3_rl_deploy
+   git commit -m "Update Lite3_rl_deploy submodule pointer"
+   git push
+   ```
+
+### How to sync later
+- To update the submodule from your fork:
+  ```bash
+  cd Lite3/Lite3_rl_deploy
+  git pull origin main
+  cd ..
+  git add Lite3_rl_deploy
+  git commit -m "Sync submodule to latest fork commit"
+  git push
+  ```
+
+### Notes
+- **Do not commit directly** to the upstream `DeepRoboticsLab/Lite3_rl_deploy`.  
+- If you want to fetch updates from upstream:
+  ```bash
+  cd Lite3/Lite3_rl_deploy
+  git fetch upstream
+  git merge upstream/main
+  git push origin main
+  ```
+- Always remember:  
+  - Submodule commits are tracked like pointers.  
+  - Both the submodule **and** the umbrella repo need a commit after changes.
+
